@dashpole good question. after thinking about it more, the apiserver's [DefaultHandlerChain](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/f97ac220fd55bbd06a37d7ab182744358df3b7ae/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/config.go#L1043) uses `filters.WithTracing` and is hit first, so it seems like maybe wrapping the handler in `proxyHandler` using `WithTracing` isn't needed outside of tests.

i updated the PR to [add a new span](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/db6182229c3833ad2b3f240aba567d889b332c31/staging/src/k8s.io/kube-aggregator/pkg/apiserver/handler_proxy.go#L108-L109) in the `proxyHandler`, and [updated the test](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/db6182229c3833ad2b3f240aba567d889b332c31/staging/src/k8s.io/kube-aggregator/pkg/apiserver/handler_proxy_test.go#L824) to wrap the `proxyHandler` in `filters.WithTracing` to simulate the filter added by `DefaultHandlerChain`.

does that seem like a better approach?
